From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jun Matsushita <jun@mercury.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:39:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] buck2_events: publish to a Bazel Build Event Service in
 OSS builds

An OSS build can stream its events to a server that speaks the Bazel Build
Event Service protocol, such as BuildBuddy. That is the role Scribe plays in
Meta's build. It is off unless [bes] is configured. The new sink code is
compiled only under cfg(not(fbcode_build)), and the shared code in
sink/scribe.rs and sink/remote.rs keeps the Scribe path under
cfg(fbcode_build).

- bazel_converter translates Buck2 events to Bazel BEP: the invocation and
  command line, targets, actions, tests, artifacts and the build graph.
- bes_client streams them over PublishBuildToolEventStream. It retries from a
  bounded replay buffer that spills to disk, and writes inline files to the
  CAS off the event path. A refused stream is not redialled, and a stalled
  connection does not block a command.
- The [bes] config takes an endpoint or the RE client's connection, plus
  headers with $VAR expansion. An unset variable turns BES off. It also
  takes a results URL, and TLS settings as the RE client has them.
- The console prints the server's results URL.
- The daemon finishes its streams before it exits.
- Snapshots report where the sink's worker spends its time.

docs/users/build_observability/event_system.md describes the configuration.

